<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="d434c706">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product covers the entire change initiative lifecycle but will be iterated to include further detail of
    business readiness and adoption activities as they become more defined:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Engagement
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section details the activities and tasks involved with executing the business change strategy via stakeholder
    engagement. It describes how the approach will become operable with planned steps, resources, milestones and timelines,
    etc. aimed to engage and manage stakeholders throughout the change process.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The engagement section of the plan provides a structured way to effectively engage, mobilize and monitor
    stakeholders. It outlines activities to motivate stakeholders that need to change as well as those that are charged
    with managing the deployment of the new solution. The plan identifies tactics to build stakeholders commitment and/or
    compliance to the change initiative.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    In general, this section describes:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Desired and current commitment levels of key stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Actions to achieve desired frequency and type of engagement for each stakeholder group
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identified interrelationships and dependencies between stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Method for updating and refining the stakeholder management plan as the project progresses
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The engagement plan  is updated during the change life cycle to reflect evolving stakeholder management
        requirements
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section defines the work activity, resources, work products and deliverables needed to execute
    the business change approach with the aim to secure the appropriate amount of buy-in or compliance to
    the changes that will result from implementing a change initiative. The plan is used as a reference and refreshed
    throughout the program lifecycle.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Readiness
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section details the activities and tasks involved with executing the Business readiness Approach. It
    describes how the approach will become operable with planned steps, resources, milestones and timelines, etc. aimed to
    prepare the business for change. It identifies all activities and tasks needed to effectively work with the
    business to plan and manage people related changes.  
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Adoption Plan
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The business adoption section specifies the actions that define, monitor and report metrics about post implementation
    stabilization and adoption of the business solution.  This section&apos;s content supports the conduct and
    monitoring of business adoption during and after implementation.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
